{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789166197,"nonce":"1QEnJLe/arhWW/i3p1pOTJ2TaXk=","message":"Fixed in the emitter, as the issue asked: `CONSTANT_ALIGN = 8`, each member of `ash_constants` padded up to it inside the member (so the index every constant GEP addresses it by does not move), and the blob aligned to `max(pointer_align, 8)`. The fallback member (an i8 array) is rounded the same way.\n\nReproducer, macOS debug profile, `test_mandelbrot_small.hl` built for wasm32-wasip1 and run under `target/debug/ash-wasm-run`:\n\n- before: `panicked at std/src/strings.rs:561:13: misaligned pointer dereference: address must be a multiple of 0x8 but is 0x817bdc` (same address as filed)\n- after: the three traces print, `Checksum: 22825041`, clean exit. The module built by the fixed emitter is byte-identical across two builds.\n\nNative layout is also padded (a member whose size is not a multiple of 8 grows), which nothing addresses by offset. `cargo test -p ash` (aot_smoke, wasm_target, cross_targets, parity_matrix, stdlib_matrix ...) and `-p ash_core` pass locally; the NUC unit suite under aot, wasm and wasm-fibers is recorded on the commit.\n\nLanded as 8726f54. NUC, same tree: unit suite 1069/1069 under aot, wasm and wasm-fibers (isolated).","files":null}]}